==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{proto|lang=ang|Germanic|fimfi}} from {{proto|Indo-European|lang=ang|penkwe|five}}. Cognates include Old High German ''fimf'', ''finf'' (German ''[[fünf]]''), Old Saxon ''fīf'' (Dutch [[vijf]]), Old Norse ''[[fimm]]'' (Swedish ''[[fem]]''), Gothic [[𐍆𐌹𐌼𐍆]].  The IE root is also the source of Greek ''[[πέντε]]'', Latin ''[[quinque]]'', Sanskrit [[पञ्चन्]].

